12 |     api.notes().get(id).await
   |                 ^^^ not an argument of type `i64`
   |
   = help: the trait `Arg<i64>` is not implemented for `i32`
   = note: an argument of type `i64` takes that type, or a reference to it when it is `Clone`, which is cloned; a `String` takes a `&str` too, and a `Vec` an array or a slice of what an item takes
   = note: no number becomes another: convert it first, with `From`, or `try_into()?` where it may not fit; an `Option<String>` takes `Some("x".into())`, and a `Vec<String>` `["a"]` rather than `vec!["a"]`
   = help: the following other types implement trait `Arg<T>`:
             `&&str` implements `Arg<String>`
             `&T` implements `Arg<T>`
             `&[A; N]` implements `Arg<Vec<T>>`
             `&[A]` implements `Arg<Vec<T>>`
             `&str` implements `Arg<String>`
             `[A; N]` implements `Arg<Vec<T>>`
